              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Alicia Knight"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Well -- we meant to make this recipe -- but accidently dumped a can of frozen orange juice instead of the lemonade. We were committed because the beer was already in the pitcher, so we added the vodka and hoped for the best. How bad could it be? Not bad at all -- actually really good! A happy mistake. We will make the regular recipe with the lemonade next -- which we've made before with tequila instead of vodka. We also did a little drizzle of grenadine to see what happened - and it made it look even prettier -- just a bit sweeter, but I like it without the grenadine just as much. Fun recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2014-08-02T18:35:14.613Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rosie G"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this drink! Everyone at my Superbowl party loved it :) I used 1 can of frozen minute maid lemonade, 3 bottles of miller lite and 6oz of vodka! Very refreshing drink! :)",
            "datePublished": "2012-02-05T18:33:13.480Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SuzyQTexas"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Our neighborhood knows this drink as \"Hop, Skip and Go Naked!\" One night of these drinks at Bunco and the husbands all renamed our fizzy margaritas. They now insist we serve them at Bunco because we all come home really happy! I only use 6 oz. of vodka instead of 8. Pour over ice and serve with lime wedges. Super drink for summer, but be careful! They will sneak up on you!",
            "datePublished": "2010-04-03T19:02:37.237Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DREGINEK"
            },
            "reviewBody": "While I prefer the lime version of this recipe - this WAS very good. It is DANGEROUS so drink with caution - especially if it’s hot out! 😂 Thanks to this recipe, now know I have a solid back up if I don’t have frozen limeade concentrate in the freezer! Thanks Michael!",
            "datePublished": "2025-05-25T17:32:15.472Z"
          },
          {
